# Code owners of the integration store.
#
# The last matching pattern wins. When a pattern lists several owners, the
# approval of any one of them is enough.
#
# Enforced only when the `main` branch protection enables "Require review from
# Code Owners"; every team listed here needs write access to the repository.

# Everything — the validation code, the JSON schemas, the workflows, the README
# (which documents the store definition) and this file — is owned by the
# maintainers.
* @GladysAssistant/maintainers

# Store data: the core team can review and merge blocklist changes (see
# "Moderation: the blocklist" in the README) and the fallback browse categories.
# Their format stays enforced by the code and the tests above.
/data/blocklist.json @GladysAssistant/maintainers @GladysAssistant/core
/data/category-fallback.json @GladysAssistant/maintainers @GladysAssistant/core
